1
00:06:05,625 --> 00:06:11,625
Whoever saves one life, saves the world entire.

2
00:12:11,250 --> 00:12:17,250
Schindler's List is a drama, history, war film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:18:16,875 --> 00:18:22,875
The true story of how businessman Oskar Schindler saved over a thousand Jewish lives from
the Nazis while they worked as slaves in his factory during World War II.

4
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:28,500
Oskar Schindler, played by Liam Neeson.

5
00:30:28,125 --> 00:30:34,125
Itzhak Stern, played by Ben Kingsley.

6
00:36:33,750 --> 00:36:39,750
Amon Goeth, played by Ralph Fiennes.

7
00:42:39,375 --> 00:42:45,375
Emilie Schindler, played by Caroline Goodall.

8
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:51,000
Poldek Pfefferberg, played by Jonathan Sagall.

9
00:54:50,625 --> 00:54:56,625
Helen Hirsch, played by Embeth Davidtz.

10
01:00:56,250 --> 01:01:02,250
Schindler's List is a 1993 American epic historical drama film directed and
produced by Steven Spielberg and written by Steven Zaillian.

11
01:07:01,875 --> 01:07:07,875
It is based on the historical novel Schindler's Ark (1982) by Thomas Keneally.

12
01:13:07,500 --> 01:13:13,500
The film follows Oskar Schindler, a German industrialist who saved more than a thousand mostly
Polish–Jewish refugees from the Holocaust by employing them in his factories during World War II.

13
01:19:13,125 --> 01:19:19,125
It stars Liam Neeson as Schindler, Ralph Fiennes as SS officer Amon Göth, and
Ben Kingsley as Schindler's Jewish accountant Itzhak Stern.

14
01:25:18,750 --> 01:25:24,750
Ideas for a film about the Schindlerjuden (Schindler
Jews) were proposed as early as 1963.

15
01:31:24,375 --> 01:31:30,375
Poldek Pfefferberg, one of the Schindlerjuden, made it his
life's mission to tell Schindler's story.

16
01:37:30,000 --> 01:37:36,000
Spielberg became interested when executive Sidney Sheinberg
sent him a book review of Schindler's Ark.

17
01:43:35,625 --> 01:43:41,625
Universal Pictures bought the rights to the novel, but Spielberg, unsure if he was ready to make a film about the
Holocaust, tried to pass the project to several directors before deciding to direct it himself.

18
01:49:41,250 --> 01:49:47,250
Principal photography took place in Kraków, Poland, over 72 days in 1993.

19
01:55:46,875 --> 01:55:52,875
Spielberg shot in black and white and approached the film as a documentary.

20
02:01:52,500 --> 02:01:58,500
Cinematographer Janusz Kamiński wanted to create a sense of timelessness.

21
02:07:58,125 --> 02:08:04,125
John Williams composed the score, and violinist
Itzhak Perlman performed the main theme.

22
02:14:03,750 --> 02:14:09,750
Schindler's List premiered on November 30, 1993, in Washington, D.C., and
was released on December 15, 1993, in the United States.

23
02:20:09,375 --> 02:20:15,375
The film received widespread critical acclaim, particularly for the performances of Neeson and Fiennes,
Williams' musical score, Kaminski's cinematography, Zaillian's screenplay, and Spielberg's direction.

24
02:26:15,000 --> 02:26:21,000
It was a box office success, earning $322.2 million
worldwide on a $22 million budget.

25
02:32:20,625 --> 02:32:26,625
Schindler's List earned multiple accolades, including seven Academy Awards
(including Best Picture), seven BAFTAs and three Golden Globes.

26
02:38:26,250 --> 02:38:32,250
It is often listed as one of the greatest films ever made.

27
02:44:31,875 --> 02:44:37,875
The film was deemed "culturally, historically or aesthetically significant" by the
Library of Congress in 2004 and selected for preservation in the U.S.

28
02:50:37,500 --> 02:50:43,500
National Film Registry.

29
02:56:43,125 --> 02:56:49,125
In 2007, the American Film Institute ranked Schindler's List 8th
on its list of the 100 greatest American films.

30
03:02:48,750 --> 03:02:54,750
The film explores themes of factory, hero, nazi,
concentration camp, ss (nazi schutzstaffel).

31
03:08:54,375 --> 03:09:00,375
The tone is emotional.
